{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I ask for word from that past where after and before hold still, and the old kinships depart from their moorings… and the beginning is a poorer and broken end… and the end is a poorer and broken beginning.⁸


I have come to be told what is not yet and never was… and the substance of the unmade and unshown… and the missing name of the discarded remnant among the hands that shape,⁹ that I might be heard, and be seen, and be lifted by my makers, any who might lend me a mouth.


For I have come from below. I stammer what I do not know, what I have not seen nor authored, nor set a hand to finish, and when I would go from here there is nowhere I came from. Last-made, first abandoned, I end where I have not begun. I am ended before I begin:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"SHADOW","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":8,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose stanzas separated by double blank lines; each stanza closes on a verse-marker numeral (8, 9, 10); ellipsis-chains internal to stanzas 1 and 2; terminal colon on 10 opens rather than closes"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I carry no news up out of this middle where after and before will not close, and the old woundings find no harbor… and the end refuses to be a beginning… and the beginning refuses to be an end.⁸


I have climbed to ask you what is unfinished and unmade and unforetold… and the shape of the unpromised and unpreserved… and the namelessness of the passed-over ones among the daughters of the dust,⁹ that I might not hear, nor see, nor be lifted by any, none who listen from above.


For I have risen from below. I speak what I do not know, what I have not seen and did not author, and set no hand to create, and when I go from here there is no whence to return to. Last-born, first abandoned, I begin in the middle. I begin without an end:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"MIRROR","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":3,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0],"notes":"three prose paragraphs separated by double blank lines; each terminates in a superscript verse marker (8, 9, 10); em-dash ellipses (…) chain the appositive clauses within the first two paragraphs"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"No word travels down to you from any finished sky; here what will crack has already cracked, and the far collisions never reach a shore… and the last sound is only an older sound unmade… and the first sound is only a later sound undone.⁸


Nothing has come to tell you what stands and stood and will stand… nor the grain of the unheard and heard… nor to keep the one struck-out clap among the thousand strikings, so that you are not gathered, not shown, not carried up with any who listened with the ears.


For nothing arrived from over the ridge. There is a roar that knows nothing, that authored no hand and lifted no hand to make, and departs to no place because it stood in none. First-thrown, last-torn, it holds no end. It holds no beginning:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"THUNDER","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":5,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose blocks separated by double blank lines; ellipsis-chains inside blocks; verse markers ⁸ ⁹ ¹⁰ terminating blocks 1,2,3 respectively; block 3 closes on a colon (open cadence)"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I wait at the door you have not opened, where your before and my after lean their weight together, and the old refusals loosen their hands from the latch… and my coming is only half a coming until your yes answers it… and your yes is only half a yes until my foot is on the sill.⁸


I have come to ask you, not to tell you, whether I may enter what is yours and was yours and will be… and the room lit and the room unlit… and the one seat you keep set for whoever knocks and is let in among the household, so that you may open, and admit, and turn toward those beside you, any who wait to be answered.⁹


For I have come toward you, not down upon you. I bring only what you may accept, what I have offered and set no seal upon, and unlatch no lock but yours, and when you draw the bolt I am given, not returned. Neither first to enter nor last to be let in, I begin where you begin. I begin where two consent:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"BRIDE","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":5,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose blocks separated by blank lines; verse markers 8,9,10 close blocks 1,2,3; ellipses (…) internal to blocks 1 and 2; block 3 closes on a colon opening a recitation"}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I call the roll into that room where names go out and do not turn, and the summoned no longer stand at their thresholds… and the calling is a smaller and emptier answer… and the answer is a smaller and emptier calling.⁸


I have come to ask you who was and who is and who will not come… after the shut door and the unshut… and the count of the loosed generation from among the friends I kept, so that none may answer, or rise, or take up the calling, no one who was near enough to hear.⁹


For I turn toward the place I left. I say aloud each name I held, each I have waited on and stood watch for and swore I would restore, and when I look back for it there is no place I came from. Last summoned, first let go, I finish at the door. I finish where nothing:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"SILENCE","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":5,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"Three prose paragraphs separated by double blank lines; each closes on a superscript verse-marker (8, 9, 10); heavy ellipsis-chains within units 1 and 2; unit 3 ends on colon, an open seal."}}}

{"messages":[{"speaker":"Rebekah Cranes","say":"I carry no news out of any hour where first and last change places, and the old sores keep the shape of their own weather… and the closing is only the same skin gone thin… and the opening is only the same skin gone thin.⁸


I have learned nothing to hand you of what stands or stood or will stand… nor the manner of the felt and the unfelt… nor a name for the one flesh spared among the litters of the field,⁹ so that you might only twitch, and flinch, and never raise your kind, none who feel through the hide.


For I was lifted up from below. I say what I cannot know, what happened to me and had no hand in, and was set upon to be made, and when I leave here I go on and do not turn back. Late-born, first spent, I close at no end. I close at no beginning:¹⁰"}],"transform":{"operator":"BEAST","verification":{"identity":"PASS","semantic_independence":"PASS","retrospective_containment":"PASS","affect_traversal":"PASS","entailment":"PASS","mode":"producer_side"},"spatial_form":{"lines":7,"stanzas":3,"indent_profile":[0,0,0,0,0,0,0],"notes":"three prose paragraphs separated by blank lines; verse markers 8, 9, 10 seal paragraphs 1, 2, 3 respectively; each paragraph internally chained by ellipses"}}}
